(7439164, 1175713, 103142, '<td valign="top">This is truly wonderful. Should have scored even higher. What a wonderful thing to explore. Huge congrats on the blue!</td>', 'This is truly wonderful. Should have scored even higher. What a wonderful thing to explore. Huge congrats on the blue!', '2016-02-23 22:13:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(7439315, 1175970, 150277, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>First off I love knowing I can say pretty much whatever I am thinking and it''ll be okay.  So thanks.<br/> <br/>And second for the critique...<br/> <br/>When I was voting I was very open with what I thought could relate to Year of the Monkey.  I tried to do a bit of reading but still did not feel I could really judge what did or did not meet the challenge.  That said a New Year is brought in with major partying all over the world it seems, so a party animal definitely fits the challenge in my mind.  <br/> <br/>Creatively I loved this.  Tutu was wonderful and the dog''s expression is priceless.  Too bad the little guy couldn''t dance on his own, the hand distracted a bit even though it made sense in the context of a dance.<br/> <br/>I thought the technicals of the image were great. I gave the image a 6 during voting.  The sharpness of the dog''s face and gentle blur of the background I found very pleasing.  I did not find anything bothersome in the processing.  The colors of the flowers added significantly to my enjoyment of this.<br/> <br/>So sorry I''m not sophisticated enough to really understand in this case how this ended up with a score below 5.  I guess maybe others had strict ideas of what did and did not meet the challenge.  I admit some of my top pics had more of a Chinese ring to them, but the technical image worthiness to your shot seemed to help your rise above others in my mind.  <br/> <br/>Keep shooting.  Glad to have you around here!</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. First off I love knowing I can say pretty much whatever I am thinking and it''ll be okay.  So thanks. And second for the critique... When I was voting I was very open with what I thought could relate to Year of the Monkey.  I tried to do a bit of reading but still did not feel I could really judge what did or did not meet the challenge.  That said a New Year is brought in with major partying all over the world it seems, so a party animal definitely fits the challenge in my mind.   Creatively I loved this.  Tutu was wonderful and the dog''s expression is priceless.  Too bad the little guy couldn''t dance on his own, the hand distracted a bit even though it made sense in the context of a dance. I thought the technicals of the image were great. I gave the image a 6 during voting.  The sharpness of the dog''s face and gentle blur of the background I found very pleasing.  I did not find anything bothersome in the processing.  The colors of the flowers added significantly to my enjoyment of this. So sorry I''m not sophisticated enough to really understand in this case how this ended up with a score below 5.  I guess maybe others had strict ideas of what did and did not meet the challenge.  I admit some of my top pics had more of a Chinese ring to them, but the technical image worthiness to your shot seemed to help your rise above others in my mind.   Keep shooting.  Glad to have you around here!', '2016-02-24 09:18:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(7441959, 1175892, 35804, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by hahn23:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by RKT:</b></div><hr/><i> An artlessly flash lit shot of hanging stuffed animals will not win my heart. Some context and better light may have gotten you something higher than the 3 I''m giving this, because at least they are on subject. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks for the generous vote of "3".  I resent your comment of "artlessly flash lit".  Who are you to say such a thing?  Oh, yeah.  I just looked at your portfolio and I see what a genuine artist you are. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Richard, you make it hard for people to like you. I never attacked you as a photographer...then you say this about me:<br/> <br/>"Who are you to say such a thing?  Oh, yeah.  I just looked at your portfolio and I see what a genuine artist you are."<br/> <br/>Not that I need to defend my opinion of this image, but I do have an actual advanced degree and have had my work exhibited internationally.<br/> <br/>This is a bad photograph, just my opinion and I can see from the other low votes I was not alone in my thinking. At least I told you why I gave this image a 3. I admire much of your photography, I really do. This was not one of the images. I never said anything about you personally and am sorry you felt the need to go after me as a photographer, and not just my photographs.</td>', 'Originally posted by hahn23: Originally posted by RKT: An artlessly flash lit shot of hanging stuffed animals will not win my heart. Some context and better light may have gotten you something higher than the 3 I''m giving this, because at least they are on subject.  Thanks for the generous vote of "3".  I resent your comment of "artlessly flash lit".  Who are you to say such a thing?  Oh, yeah.  I just looked at your portfolio and I see what a genuine artist you are.   Richard, you make it hard for people to like you. I never attacked you as a photographer...then you say this about me: "Who are you to say such a thing?  Oh, yeah.  I just looked at your portfolio and I see what a genuine artist you are." Not that I need to defend my opinion of this image, but I do have an actual advanced degree and have had my work exhibited internationally. This is a bad photograph, just my opinion and I can see from the other low votes I was not alone in my thinking. At least I told you why I gave this image a 3. I admire much of your photography, I really do. This was not one of the images. I never said anything about you personally and am sorry you felt the need to go after me as a photographer, and not just my photographs.', '2016-03-08 14:17:56.000000', NULL, 0);
COMMIT;
